  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The function $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=(\\mathrm{x}(\\mathrm{x}-2))^{2}$ is increasing in the set",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "l3u9R",
      "text": "$(-\\infty, 0) \\cup(2, \\infty)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NJyxr",
      "text": "$(-\\infty, 1)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lP0Kn",
      "text": "(0,1)$\\cup(2, \\infty)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b9h6H",
      "text": "(1,2)",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\r\n\r\n\\text { } \\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\text { Here, } \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=(\\mathrm{x}(\\mathrm{x}-2))^{2} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(\\mathrm{x})=4 \\mathrm{x}(\\mathrm{x}-2)(\\mathrm{x}-1)\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nFor $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})$ as increasing, $\\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(\\mathrm{x})>0$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\text { So, } 4 x(x-1)(x-2)>0 \\Rightarrow x(x-1)(x-2)>0\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/lSKQqu4_r-O0TQCuFzGXYtr4R0q6W-FA-qe_tBAQ7TI.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nFrom the above figure required interval is, (0,1)$\\cup(2, \\infty)$",
    "image": null
  },
